/**
 * Social studies records (Phase 3) — the single validated content source
 * for social studies.
 *
 * Generated by gen/gen-records.mts from the pre-move exports of this
 * file and ./answers.ts (the unit fields read from
 * docs/scaling/social-studies/items.json by the old adapter, which never
 * edited that data file). Content bytes come from those inputs only:
 * do not hand-edit a record here, and do not retype one. The records
 * are verified by the frozen-fixture test against
 * __fixtures__/main-38468953.json, captured from the old exports.
 * The next social-studies PR deletes the answers.ts compatibility export.
 *
 * Each record is one SubjectItem: the UnitItem fields (contract I2) plus its
 * answer, provenance, media rules and lead policy. Screens read projections
 * of these records (socialStudiesUnits, answerFor); they never join files
 * by hand. Provenance is UNVERIFIED for all 12 records: no verifiedOn date
 * exists for these rows. Media is empty for all 12: social studies carries
 * no clip or still ids today. Lead policy is answer-not-in-lead for every
 * record.
 *
 * The slice keeps up to 3 items per age band, picked where the row's
 * why / objective yields one unambiguous multiple-choice answer with
 * the shared AnswerCard. Every item was re-screened against
 * docs/scaling/humanities/screened-topics.md: the shipped items are
 * map and route geography only (directions H04, routes H03, landform
 * geography H18 — KEEP / KEEP-LIMITS), with settled facts only. No
 * religion, no contested politics, no biology. Items that need a map
 * in front of the player (pin drops, sorting pictured places,
 * comparing by eye) are held for a later wave; see the PR body.
 *
 * The v2 wave re-screened every unplayed row against the same list
 * and added the rows whose why yields one unambiguous verbal answer:
 * compass-clue (7-10, directions H04 — asked in words here; the
 * pin-drop form stays with the map mode), fastest-or-shortest and
 * time-zones (10-18, routes H03 — both deferred in v1 only because
 * travel-time had not shipped yet; time zones follow from longitude).
 * Per-band counts are now 4 (7-10), 5 (10-18), 3 (18+). Still held:
 * grid-reference, landform-sort, farther-or-nearer, latlon-pin and
 * compass-bearing; see the PR body.
 *
 * Deal order: SOCIAL_STUDIES_ITEM_IDS below — the live slice, in deal
 * order per band (v1 slice, then the v2 wave).
 */
